    Section(
      title: 'History & Systems Review:',
      content:
          '- **Oncologic History**: Right breast invasive ductal carcinoma, ER+/PR-/HER2+, Stage IIIA. Treated with neoadjuvant AC-TH (doxorubicin/cyclophosphamide, then docetaxel/trastuzumab), right MRM with ALND (18 nodes removed, 4/18 positive), adjuvant chest wall and regional nodal radiation (50 Gy), completing trastuzumab, and now on letrozole (aromatase inhibitor). Last imaging (PET/CT) 3 months ago showed no evidence of recurrence.\n- **Lymphedema Timeline**: First noticed right hand puffiness at 18 months post-surgery. Progressive involvement of forearm, then entire arm. No precipitating event (no injury, infection, or air travel at onset).\n- **Infections**: Two episodes of right arm cellulitis — treated with cephalexin each time. No hospitalizations for cellulitis.\n- **Functional Impact**: Difficulty with overhead reaching, carrying objects >5 lbs with right arm, prolonged painting/drawing causes increased swelling. Has modified teaching to rely more on verbal instruction.\n- **BMI**: 31.2 (obese). Weight has increased 10 kg since completing chemotherapy.\n- **Comorbidities**: Hypertension, prediabetes (HbA1c 6.2%), osteopenia (letrozole-related), chemotherapy-induced amenorrhea\n- **Medications**: Letrozole 2.5 mg daily, lisinopril 10 mg daily, metformin 500 mg BID, calcium/vitamin D, acetaminophen PRN\n- **Previous Lymphedema Treatment**: Wore an off-the-shelf compression sleeve (20-30 mmHg) for 2 months — discontinued because it was uncomfortable and did not seem to help. No formal CDT.\n- **Psychosocial**: Married, 2 teenage children. Works full-time as art teacher. Previously very active socially. Now avoids sleeveless tops, avoids pool parties, stopped wearing her wedding ring (does not fit right hand). PHQ-9 score 12 (moderate depression).',
