      content:
          '**Vitals**: BP 138/84 mmHg, HR 72 bpm, RR 14, SpO2 99% on RA, Temp 36.7C, BMI 31.2.\n\n**Right Upper Extremity**:\n- **Inspection**: Diffuse swelling from hand to axilla. Loss of normal anatomic contours at wrist and elbow. Skin thickened with peau d\'orange texture over dorsum of hand and forearm. Positive **Stemmer sign** (inability to pinch and lift a skin fold at the base of the second toe/finger — in this case, unable to tent skin at base of right 2nd digit). No skin breakdown. Well-healed mastectomy scar. No erythema or warmth to suggest active cellulitis.\n- **Circumferential Measurements** (compared to left):\n  - Hand (metacarpal): R 22.5 cm, L 19.0 cm (+3.5 cm)\n  - Wrist: R 19.0 cm, L 16.5 cm (+2.5 cm)\n  - Forearm (10 cm below olecranon): R 30.0 cm, L 25.5 cm (+4.5 cm)\n  - Elbow: R 31.0 cm, L 27.0 cm (+4.0 cm)\n  - Upper arm (10 cm above olecranon): R 38.0 cm, L 32.0 cm (+6.0 cm)\n- **Volume**: Estimated right arm volume excess approximately 35-40% compared to left (by truncated cone formula).\n- **Tissue Consistency**: Pitting edema present at hand and forearm with slow rebound (>10 seconds). Non-pitting, fibrotic tissue at upper arm with firm induration.\n- **ROM**: Right shoulder flexion 140 degrees (limited by tissue bulk), abduction 120 degrees. Elbow, wrist, and hand ROM functionally full but limited by swelling.\n- **Strength**: Right grip 18 kg (left 28 kg). Right shoulder and elbow strength 4+/5 (limited by heaviness and fatigue).\n\n**Left Upper Extremity**: Normal. No swelling.\n\n**Chest Wall**: Right mastectomy scar well-healed. Mild chest wall lymphedema with thickened skin in right axillary fold. Radiation skin changes (hyperpigmentation, telangiectasia) over right anterior chest.\n\n**Vascular**: Radial and ulnar pulses 2+ bilaterally. No axillary or supraclavicular lymphadenopathy. No venous distension.\n\n**Neurologic**: Intact sensation bilaterally. No signs of brachial plexopathy.',
